{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/426532-greenland-lost-hunter-dark-era-idea","id":426532,"title":"Greenland Lost (Hunter Dark Era idea)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-03T06:57:19-08:00","id":426532,"title":"Greenland Lost (Hunter Dark Era idea)","content":"<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Starting in the Tenth Century, Vikings settled the southern part of Greenland, In the Thirteenth Century, </span></span></span><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inuit\" target=\"_blank\">Inuit</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> peoples joined the Norsemen in calling Greenland home. In the late Fifteenth Century, the Norse colonies disappeared. The last report to the world at large from the Norse colonies was in 1410. However, some scholars think there was contact between Europe and Greenland as last as 1480. Whatever the case, by the close of the Fifteenth Century, the Norse colonies vanished into history. Just why this happened remains a <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/\" target=\"_blank\">contested<img src=\"http://cdncache-a.akamaihd.net/items/it/img/arrow-10x10.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a> mystery. However, the truth is far more awful than most modern scholars would ever imagine. For it was nothing less than monsters that brought about the destruction of the Norse colonies. However, these monsters were not unchallenged. In those dark days, the last remnants of the Norse colonies fought along side the Inuit against a rising tide of monsters determined to see both groups destroyed.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  left out words 03-03-2015, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T22:17:16-08:00","id":429833,"title":"","content":"Do you have suggestion on era appropriate Norse Hunter groups?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:17:11-08:00","id":430237,"title":"","content":"Good question, Glamourweaver. I guess I envisioned more a cell level type of thing, but it occurs to me that the Aegis Kai Doru may well have taken advantage of Greenland's relative isolation from Europe to hide what they wanted hidden. I think that there also could have been a Lucifuge presence in Greenland as well. I have read that Inuit have legends of forces from Europe attacking and destroying the Norse colonies (although I do not think there is evidence for this). One possible take on this legend is that Malleus Maleficarum had come to find what ever evil force had beset the Norse colonies. Another possible but darker take is that after 1410, a revival to the Norse religion was taking place, and that the Malleus Maleficarum had come to deal with that.<br /> <br /> I also think it would be nice to have some compacts specific to Greenland of this time. I am giving it some thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:10:23-08:00","id":430289,"title":"","content":"just a very very rough idea : Guardians of Hyperborea ,a Compact who belives , that Greenland was a former Paradise (lost garden of Eden?) wich they must protect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T11:36:16-08:00","id":430471,"title":"","content":"I like it. I think it fits well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T13:17:21-07:00","id":451966,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea: Some sources from the middle ages identify the legendary &quot;Thule&quot; as Iceland or Greenland. Perhaps whatever takes place in the last days of the Nordic Colonies is the speck of truth that informs the myths that serve as the foundation for the Society of Thule so many centuries later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T13:28:13-07:00","id":451980,"title":"","content":"Wow. I had not thought of that!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T16:11:00-07:00","id":452112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps whatever takes place in the last days of the Nordic Colonies is the speck of truth that informs the myths that serve as the foundation for the Society of Thule so many centuries later. </div> </div> </div>A difficulty I could see with that is that the Thule Society was a real society and we know exactly where they got the ideas from. Plus the underlying point of the Loyalists is that though they stumbled into the supernatural, the Thule Society was fundmentally wrong in their starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T20:42:05-07:00","id":453748,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, did not the Thule Soceity not believe in something like a hallow earth? Perhaps there could supposedly be like an opening to such a place in Greenland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}